\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces Multi-asset extension via the Single-Index Model (SIM) across 424 S\&P\nonbreakingspace 500 constituents. Panel\nonbreakingspace (a) summarises the SIM regression fit quality by GICS sector. Panel\nonbreakingspace (b) shows that KS distributional consistency is maintained across the full asset universe when paths are generated via the factor structure $\hat  {G}_{i,t} = \hat  {\alpha }_i + \hat  {\beta }_i G_{{\rm  SPY},t} + \hat  {\eta }_{i,t}$. Panel\nonbreakingspace (c) illustrates representative marginal density comparisons for three assets spanning a wide range of systematic risk exposure.}}{16}{figure.caption.17}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:multi_asset}{{5}{16}{Multi-asset extension via the Single-Index Model (SIM) across 424 S\&P~500 constituents. Panel~(a) summarises the SIM regression fit quality by GICS sector. Panel~(b) shows that KS distributional consistency is maintained across the full asset universe when paths are generated via the factor structure $\hat {G}_{i,t} = \hat {\alpha }_i + \hat {\beta }_i G_{{\rm SPY},t} + \hat {\eta }_{i,t}$. Panel~(c) illustrates representative marginal density comparisons for three assets spanning a wide range of systematic risk exposure}{figure.caption.17}{}}
